WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.940
I have a really important case study for you
today about how Republicans end up muddying

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.130
the waters and winning merely by distracting.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:12.230
As you probably know, Donald Trump has been
impeached.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:17.370
We have an impeached president, only the third
in the history of the United States.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:22.670
We are now standing by for the Senate trial,
which will begin when SA a house speaker,

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:27.090
Nancy Pelosi sends the impeachment articles
that the house approved over to the Senate

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.820
and acquittal is all but a foregone conclusion
in the Republican controlled Senate.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.430
I've talked about how it could go differently.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.420
It's not likely to go differently.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:39.620
This is all about Donald Trump, but Republicans
have been able to turn this around and make

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:46.460
it about Joe Biden during the last week, democratic
primary candidate and former VP Joe Biden

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:52.500
said to the Des Moines register last week,
he would not comply if the Senate subpoenas

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.219
him to the impeachment trial of Donald Trump
in the Senate.

00:00:56.219 --> 00:01:02.989
Now, Joe Biden accurately told the newspaper
that sending a subpoena to Joe Biden would

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:07.220
be a way to take attention off of Trump and
that part he was right about.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.690
But then he said that he wouldn't comply.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:14.250
And of course, Joe Biden is right that subpoenaing
him to the impeachment trial would be an attempt

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.620
to distract from Donald Trump.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:20.540
But immediately Republicans respond with,
how could this be?

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:24.700
Biden would ignore a subpoena, even though
Democrats won't stop talking about how Republicans

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.050
are ignoring subpoenas and they're terrible
because of it.

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:32.590
This Joe Biden not care about the constitution,
which is obvious concern trolling, but it

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:37.720
pushes the story to being about Biden instead
of being about Trump.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:42.530
So then this leads to another round of Biden
talking about this.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:47.120
Having to clarify Biden a few days later,
had to go back and say, well, hold on.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:52.230
Of course I would obey a legal constitutional
subpoena tweeting about it.

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:56.360
In addition to talking about it, saying on
Twitter quote, I want to clarify something

00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:01.310
I said yesterday in my 40 years in public
life, I have always complied with a lawful

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:08.440
order and in my eight years as VP, my office,
unlike Donald Trump and Mike Pence, cooperated

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.709
with legitimate congressional oversight requests.

00:02:11.709 --> 00:02:16.129
But I am not just going to pretend that there
is any legal basis for Republican subpoenas

00:02:16.129 --> 00:02:19.159
for my testimony in the impeachment trial.

00:02:19.159 --> 00:02:22.680
That is the point I was making yesterday and
I reiterate this.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.730
Impeachment is about Trump's conduct, not
mine.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:29.379
The subpoenas should go to witnesses with
testimony to offer to Trump's shaking down

00:02:29.379 --> 00:02:35.540
the Ukraine government, so now it gets more
muddled with commentary about the commentary.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:37.180
Joe Biden said he wouldn't comply.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:40.349
Then he said, of course he would comply, but
what I mean is it wouldn't make any sense

00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:41.989
to subpoena me.

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:44.380
Republicans are great at this and Biden's
stepped in it.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:49.040
What Biden should have said from day one is
this impeachment trial has nothing to do with

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.040
me.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:54.189
Any attempt to pull me into it would be an
attempt to distract.

00:02:54.189 --> 00:02:59.069
Of course, I believe in the constitution and
the rule of law and I will always do what

00:02:59.069 --> 00:03:04.760
is legally required of me, but the idea that
I should be part of this Senate trial is a

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:10.599
political strategy make to meant to make impeachment
about me instead of about Donald Trump.

00:03:10.599 --> 00:03:11.639
He didn't say that.

00:03:11.639 --> 00:03:13.969
Instead, he sort of tried to be tough.

00:03:13.969 --> 00:03:16.469
I won't go, but that's the wrong thing to
say.

00:03:16.469 --> 00:03:17.889
He has to walk it back.

00:03:17.889 --> 00:03:19.989
They are experts, experts in this.

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:22.659
They won't even fight the substance.

00:03:22.659 --> 00:03:25.379
They distract, misdirect.

00:03:25.379 --> 00:03:28.029
They get Democrats to argue with themselves.

00:03:28.029 --> 00:03:29.180
We've got to be smarter.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.129
We can't be falling for this stuff.

00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:33.409
And Joe Biden did remember that.

